# canvas-ycu: a stale local incremental-build cache left over from a plain `tsc -p` invocation
# (composite: true in every package's tsconfig.json) fools a later build into thinking it's
# already up to date and silently emitting nothing, even with dist/ itself excluded above --
# discovered building this Dockerfile against a working tree with leftover *.tsbuildinfo files.
# canvas-ycu.1: the bare `*.tsbuildinfo` pattern above only ever matched a build-context-ROOT
# file, exactly like `node_modules`/`dist` on their own (lines 1/3/5/7 above) needed their own
# `**/` sibling line -- unlike .gitignore, a plain dockerignore pattern with no `**/` prefix does
# NOT match at any depth. packages/diagram-core/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo (created by any ordinary
# local `npm run build`) was silently slipping through into every real `docker build`/`az acr
# build` since canvas-ycu shipped, undetected until a from-scratch --no-cache build was actually
# exercised for canvas-ycu.1 -- confirmed via a minimal isolated dockerignore repro, not guessed.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
